WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.780
A new question. What happens when the photoreceptors themselves die?

2
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:14.030
In typical retinitis pigmentosa, the faulty gene is often not expressed in cones.

3
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:20.613
Predict. If the faulty gene is not expressed in cones, should the cones be spared?

4
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:31.667
No. They die too, typically after most of the rods around them have gone.

5
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.340
Patients typically lose night vision first, then peripheral vision.

6
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.500
Central vision goes later, when cones fail.

7
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.580
So cones depend in some way on rods.

8
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.300
And cones carry daylight, colour and sharp central vision.

9
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.190
Why cones die is not settled.

10
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.070
One candidate is lost support from rods.

11
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:57.773
Rods make a rod-derived cone viability factor, called RdCVF.

12
00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:04.157
In chicken cone cultures and a mouse model, RdCVF binds basigin-1.

13
00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:09.407
Basigin one associates with a glucose transporter, and cone glucose entry rises.

14
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.180
Cone starvation and oxidative damage are other candidates.

15
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.620
Can vision be rescued?

16
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.620
Gene therapy has begun to improve vision in specific genetic forms.

17
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:25.813
One trial added a working RPE65 gene.

18
00:01:26.593 --> 00:01:30.933
It was randomized and open-label, with masked grading of a mobility test.

19
00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:37.766
At one year, treated participants did better than controls, by 1.6 light levels.

20
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.010
A later study delivered editing machinery for CEP290 inside the eye.

21
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.810
It had no randomized or sham control, only the untreated fellow eye.

22
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:54.963
It recorded no dose-limiting toxic effects during follow-up, and signs of possible

23
00:01:54.963 --> 00:01:55.963
benefit.

24
00:01:56.466 --> 00:01:59.426
The fellow eye shares the person and the testing days.

25
00:02:00.226 --> 00:02:05.206
But practice, expectation and fluctuation cannot be fully separated from treatment.

26
00:02:06.266 --> 00:02:09.386
The takeaway. The design limits the claim.

27
00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:13.786
The randomized trial supports a benefit on its mobility test.

28
00:02:14.646 --> 00:02:18.706
A small single arm supports observed safety and a preliminary signal.
